{"name":"Melancholic Sea","hex":"#53778f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"melancholic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Filled with or affected by melancholy—great sadness or depression, especially of a thoughtful or introspective nature.","Pertaining to black bile (melancholy)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is habitually melancholy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melancholic"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Melancholia","blocks":[{"text":"Melancholia or melancholy is a concept found throughout ancient, medieval, and premodern medicine in Europe that describes a condition characterized by markedly depressed mood, bodily complaints, and sometimes hallucinations and delusions. Besides a pathological condition, melancholy could also refer to a mood or temperament and at times it was even used as a description of the human condition in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/A_man_whose_face_exemplifies_the_melancholy_temperament._Dra_Wellcome_V0009108ER.jpg/330px-A_man_whose_face_exemplifies_the_melancholy_temperament._Dra_Wellcome_V0009108ER.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melancholia"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg/1280px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg/500px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_%28_AGDdr3EHmNGyA%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Melencolia I by Albrecht Dürer, 1514","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Melencolia_I_-_Google_Art_Project_(_AGDdr3EHmNGyA).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Robert_Burton%27s_Anatomy_of_Melancholy%2C_1626%2C_2nd_edition.jpg/500px-Robert_Burton%27s_Anatomy_of_Melancholy%2C_1626%2C_2nd_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Robert_Burton%27s_Anatomy_of_Melancholy%2C_1626%2C_2nd_edition.jpg/1280px-Robert_Burton%27s_Anatomy_of_Melancholy%2C_1626%2C_2nd_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Robert_Burton%27s_Anatomy_of_Melancholy%2C_1626%2C_2nd_edition.jpg/500px-Robert_Burton%27s